<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grito do Ipiranga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Brazilian independence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grito do Ipiranga was the declaration of Brazilian independence from Portugal made by Prince Pedro near the Ipiranga stream in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a> in 1822. Pedro was soon acclaimed as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-i-of-brazil">Emperor Pedro I</a>. The event marks the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> and the loss of Portugal's most valuable colony, a major moment in the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p></div>
